# Template drift allowlist for zudo-tauri-wisdom.
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file lists
# intentional divergences from the pinned create-zudo-doc baseline so
# `pnpm check:template-drift` exits 0.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Reconciled against create-zudo-doc 5.13.1. Non-allowlisted scaffold files
# remain byte-identical to the pinned template; the five paths below diverge
# intentionally. The drift check scans templates/base plus the i18n feature.
#
# pages/index.tsx was listed until 4.4.13 and is deliberately NOT listed now:
# the wide home grid needed a hand-reconstructed route only while zudo-doc had
# no toggle for it (zudolab/zudo-doc#2959). 4.4.x ships `home.wide`, so the
# config carries the intent and the file is back to the locked 1-line re-export
# — one fewer host file to keep reconciled on every future bump.

# ── Host customization: brand + tight-token global.css ────────────────────
# global.css carries this site's font overrides (Noto Sans JP body + Futura
# display face) and the [data-header-logo] brand rule on top of the package's
# theme.css/content.css/features.css imports.
src/styles/global.css

# ── Generator patch: docHistory-wired doc-route stubs ─────────────────────
# The docHistory feature makes the generator patch both doc-route stubs to
# statically import DocHistory and merge it into createChrome's hostBindings
# (without the patch the doc-history button never hydrates on these routes).
# The patched stubs therefore diverge from the unpatched templates/base +
# features/i18n copies.
pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx

# ── Host customization: doc-lookup skill generator ────────────────────────
# scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh is customized with this site's skill name
# (tauri-wisdom) and Claude + Codex targets, so it diverges from the template
# default. The skill it emits is gitignored.
#
# NOTE (5.13.1): upstream includes nested-project / worktree correctness — PROJECT_PREFIX,
# REPO_DOCS_DIR, MAIN_PROJECT_DIR and package.json-driven format-script
# detection (zudolab/zudo-doc#2918) — so the emitted SKILL.md points at the main
# worktree's project dir instead of the current worktree. Our fork predates all
# of that and still hard-codes `$REPO_ROOT/src/content/docs` and `pnpm
# format:md`. Deliberately NOT adopted here: porting it means re-forking a
# heavily customized file, which is a separate piece of work from a version
# bump. Recorded so it is not silently lost.
scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh

# ── Minified HTML compatibility: check-links.js ───────────────────────────
# zfb production HTML emits unquoted href/id attributes. The 5.13.1 scaffold
# checker only recognizes quoted values, so this local patch adds unquoted
# parsing plus entity decoding, covered by scripts/check-links.test.mjs. The
# unquoted token excludes backslashes so escaped serialized demo markup is not
# mistaken for a live link. Tracked upstream as zudolab/zudo-doc#3720.
scripts/check-links.js
